null, "rationale": "Refused statements, AI-CLASSIFIED statements, interpolated identifiers (an injection surface if the value can reach a caller), empty xs-security.json scopes, mta.yaml foreign-schema stubs, and runtime testing \u2014 cds build proves the model compiles, it does not run a single SQL statement."}, {"id": "docs_usage_sql_identifier_interpolated", "label": "SQL_IDENTIFIER_INTERPOLATED", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/USAGE.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "These statements did convert; SQL cannot bind an identifier, so a table or column name is written into the SQL text. Whether that value is reachable is a judgement about the whole application, so the tool names the expression rather than deciding."}, {"id": "docs_usage_exit_codes", "label": "Exit codes", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/USAGE.md", "source_location": "\u00a78", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "docs_usage_troubleshooting", "label": "Troubleshooting table", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/USAGE.md", "source_location": "\u00a77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Notable case: DUPLICATE_FUNCTION is a NEO defect the conversion exposes \u2014 a file declaring one function twice, which an XSJS script allows and an ES module rejects."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_usage_inventory_command", "target": "src_index_inventory", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/USAGE.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_usage_inventory_command", "target": "src_report_render_renderinventory", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/USAGE.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "doc